s and Promotions", "section": "Common Misreadings", "score": 0.12765263, "is_invented_example": false, "text": "A frequent misreading reports revenue lift as success. Another compares a promotion with the preceding week without recognizing that the preceding week may have been unusually strong or weak. A third attributes all sales during the window to the promotion, although a large share would have occurred anyway."}}

